/T (Ask one question at a time. Use short, clear sentences \(especially for ESL patients\).  Reflect back what you heard to confirm accuracy.  Document key quotes only when clinically meaningful.  Keep a calm tone; your demeanor affects patient regulation. If safety concerns arise, pause the interview and prioritize risk assessment.)
